The project virtualenv is `.venv` in this worktree. The README and tool-error tests were run with that interpreter, and the full suite finished with 38 passed.
The original PER-7 orchestrator uppercased every string `id` with `value.upper()` and no format check. Hyphenated and unhyphenated ids are both supported, so `_normalize_id()` keeps that rule.

Supported examples now documented in the README setup and usage sections:

- `emp-001`, `Emp-001`, `EMP-001` → `EMP-001`
- `emp001`, `Emp001` → `EMP001`
- `so-123` → `SO-123`, `so123` → `SO123`
- `ord-001` → `ORD-001`
- Other string ids are uppercased the same way (`foo-bar-123` → `FOO-BAR-123`, `emp_001` → `EMP_001`)

