Story 04-agent is already in the tree, and the FastMCP SSE check the review asked for is already in place. No files were changed.

`README.md` documents the FastAPI path: set `MCP_URL` to the SSE endpoint (`http://127.0.0.1:8000/sse`), set `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` or `LLM_GATEWAY_URL`, start `uvicorn agent.main:app`, and `POST /query`. It lists all four tools, the `prefix-digits` ID examples (`emp-001` → `EMP-001`, `so-123` → `SO-123`), and the health response. Flask and stdio are not mentioned. The ID section matches the client, which uppercases any string `id`.

`tests/test_tool_call.py` does not mock `httpx.post`. It starts the `mcp` library's FastMCP SSE server and checks the real session: `GET /sse` with `Accept: text/event-stream`, then `initialize`, `notifications/initialized`, and `tools/call` on `/messages/?session_id=...`. A JSON-RPC POST straight to the SSE URL is rejected and does not run a tool.

`tests/test_readme_setup.py` and `tests/test_tool_call.py` passed (11 tests). The full suite passed earlier (69 tests).
Story 04-agent now documents the FastAPI setup and the ID rule from `agent/mcp_client.py::_normalize_id`.

